  "answer_text": "An HA split-brain condition is when both Sockets have the Master role at the same time, usually caused by a LAN connectivity issue that stops HA keepalive messages from reaching the secondary. In CMA you recognise this on the Socket page: both the primary and secondary Sockets are shown as Master and the Keepalive status is indicated. During a split-brain, the traffic for the site is handled by the secondary Socket (downstream traffic is routed to the secondary, and upstream traffic follows depending on the Master status).",
